$ npm run build            exit=0   BUILD_ID Xh7-umLcPW6vE-EVOjOYB
$ node .next/standalone/server.js  (health 200)

  request (signed-in outsider, first account's workspace id)  http  audit lines
  ---------------------------------------------------------   ----  -----------
  PAGE /workspaces/<id>?organizationId=<the OTHER tenant's>    404       1
    → operation=workspacePageActor category=ORGANIZATION_NOT_FOUND
      stage=organization_unavailable actorId=cmtm6wkgo… organizationId=cmtm6v4dq…
  PAGE /workspaces/<id>   (no organizationId)                  404       1
    → operation=WorkspaceService.get category=WORKSPACE_NOT_FOUND
      stage=workspace_unavailable  workspaceId=cmtm6vbvh…
  API  /api/workspaces/<id>                                    404       1
    → operation=WorkspaceService.get category=WORKSPACE_NOT_FOUND
  PAGE /workspaces/<id>   (no session at all)                  307       0

  leaks-other-tenant-name: 0 in all four bodies
  and the owner is unaffected: first account → own Workspace, http=200, name present

The `organizationId` in the first line is the id the URL NAMED — the other
tenant's — which is the field that makes the line worth having.

── the probe's two console-reading rows, after this ────────────────────
They now report NOT EXERCISED with the reason unless `--dev-log-forwarding` is
passed, and under that flag the ids-only row additionally requires the lines to
exist before asserting what is absent from them. One false red and one vacuous
green, both removed. The probe's origin argument also now tolerates flags.

